1
00:00:06,211 --> 00:00:07,312
Good morning!

2
00:00:07,378 --> 00:00:10,548
Let's make today a good day too.

3
00:00:13,318 --> 00:00:14,886
<i>To my beloved wife.</i>

4
00:00:15,453 --> 00:00:17,755
<i>June is almost over.</i>

5
00:00:17,822 --> 00:00:19,624
<i>Are you taking care of your health?</i>

6
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:24,529
<i>As for me, the other day,</i>
<i>I was framed for something I didn't do</i>

7
00:00:24,596 --> 00:00:26,998
<i>and almost got fired, but…</i>

8
00:00:27,532 --> 00:00:31,035
<i>I was saved, thanks to</i>
<i>the help of a fellow teacher.</i>

9
00:00:31,102 --> 00:00:32,437
<i>So don't worry.</i>

10
00:00:32,504 --> 00:00:33,371
Happy bday.

11
00:00:33,438 --> 00:00:35,006
-Congratulations!
-Congratulations!

12
00:00:35,073 --> 00:00:36,341
Congratulations!

13
00:00:43,181 --> 00:00:44,149
Hey!

14
00:00:44,215 --> 00:00:45,483
Already at it this early?

15
00:00:46,251 --> 00:00:48,219
-Onicchi!
-Good morning!

16
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:49,287
Good morning!

17
00:00:49,354 --> 00:00:52,524
Huh? Momocchi, you joined the Drill Team?

18
00:00:54,058 --> 00:00:56,895
Only one more person left
until we can become official!

19
00:00:57,996 --> 00:01:00,265
Man, I worked really hard, you know.

20
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:02,834
Don't act like you gathered
all of us by yourself!

21
00:01:03,768 --> 00:01:06,538
Hey, don't walk
while staring at your phone.

22
00:01:06,604 --> 00:01:08,740
Follow the rules,
or you'll get your phone confiscated.

23
00:01:08,806 --> 00:01:09,641
Okay.

24
00:01:10,375 --> 00:01:13,511
Talk to me if you have any problems.
That's why I'm here, after all.

25
00:01:14,145 --> 00:01:15,680
So enthusiastic, Mr. Murayama.

26
00:01:16,347 --> 00:01:18,049
I'm their counselor, after all.

27
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:20,385
Come on, we have to head to class.

28
00:01:20,451 --> 00:01:21,519
Okay!

29
00:01:21,586 --> 00:01:22,954
-You practicing drills?
-Yes.

30
00:01:23,021 --> 00:01:24,189
Teach me too.

31
00:01:25,924 --> 00:01:29,260
<i>As for the answer to your homework,</i>
<i>"What makes a Great Teacher"…</i>

32
00:01:29,928 --> 00:01:32,030
It's been a while
since she texted me first.

33
00:01:33,865 --> 00:01:37,402
What? It's just my mom…

34
00:01:37,468 --> 00:01:39,204
ALOHA
AZUSA TOLD ME SHE WENT BACK HOME

35
00:01:39,270 --> 00:01:42,907
"What are you doing?
You made your wonderful wife cry."

36
00:01:42,974 --> 00:01:46,344
No! I'm the one who wants to cry!

37
00:01:51,649 --> 00:01:52,850
Excuse me…

38
00:01:54,686 --> 00:01:56,888
Principal, is something wrong?

39
00:01:56,955 --> 00:01:57,922
No…

40
00:01:58,856 --> 00:02:01,626
I was just admiring your bike.

41
00:02:02,193 --> 00:02:03,194
Right?

42
00:02:03,261 --> 00:02:07,398
Look right here, see?
It has my name engraved on it.

43
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:08,666
It really does!

44
00:02:09,334 --> 00:02:11,336
Also, check this out. Can you see?

45
00:02:11,402 --> 00:02:14,305
The "Z2" marking right here.

46
00:02:14,372 --> 00:02:16,641
It's authentic…

47
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:21,346
-Shouldn't you get going soon?
-What?

48
00:02:21,412 --> 00:02:25,049
-The staff meeting is about to start.
-Oh, shoot! See you!

49
00:02:27,318 --> 00:02:29,287
<i>That man is a mystery.</i>

50
00:02:30,021 --> 00:02:31,155
<i>He's over 50,</i>

51
00:02:31,756 --> 00:02:34,592
<i>so why is he always</i>
<i>fooling around like a child?</i>

52
00:02:36,027 --> 00:02:37,862
<i>As for me, I hit retirement age last year,</i>

53
00:02:38,763 --> 00:02:42,667
<i>but my company appointed me Principal</i>
<i>of this school they manage.</i>

54
00:02:43,301 --> 00:02:45,903
<i>Every day, I'm faced</i>
<i>with puzzling questions.</i>

55
00:02:46,704 --> 00:02:48,806
<i>This man, the Vice Principal, told me…</i>

56
00:02:49,407 --> 00:02:52,844
<i>"You don't need</i>
<i>to do anything, Principal."</i>

57
00:02:53,778 --> 00:02:55,747
<i>I don't even know</i>

58
00:02:56,881 --> 00:02:59,817
<i>what my job is supposed to be.</i>

59
00:03:00,818 --> 00:03:03,288
Is something the matter, Principal?

60
00:03:03,354 --> 00:03:07,458
No, I was just wondering
what you were talking about.

61
00:03:07,525 --> 00:03:12,830
I was just talking about
why our school is so wonderful.

62
00:03:12,897 --> 00:03:13,831
Is that so?

63
00:03:13,898 --> 00:03:17,001
The greatness of our Seishin High

64
00:03:17,702 --> 00:03:20,938
lies in our cutting-edge classes,
wonderful learning environment,

65
00:03:21,005 --> 00:03:24,108
and the overflowing passion
of all the teachers,

66
00:03:24,175 --> 00:03:25,843
especially me!

67
00:03:26,344 --> 00:03:27,745
Don't you agree, Principal?

68
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,714
You're right.

69
00:03:30,348 --> 00:03:33,384
<i>Every time I try to say something…</i>

70
00:03:34,018 --> 00:03:35,987
<i>this man interrupts me,</i>

71
00:03:36,654 --> 00:03:42,760
<i>causing my presence at this school</i>
<i>to get fainter every day.</i>

72
00:03:43,728 --> 00:03:48,166
Therefore, moving forward, I ask
all of you to act as one, with discipline…

73
00:03:50,802 --> 00:03:52,503
So noisy. What's with you?

74
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,404
Sorry!

75
00:03:54,005 --> 00:03:57,909
I dreamed I got good ratings
from the entire class.

76
00:03:57,975 --> 00:03:59,410
But maybe it's not a dream?

77
00:04:01,045 --> 00:04:02,980
Huh? Come on…

78
00:04:03,047 --> 00:04:05,216
Still only four good ratings.
No change at all…

79
00:04:08,953 --> 00:04:12,357
Among us teachers, there is one
unacceptable exception,

80
00:04:14,726 --> 00:04:20,031
but my trust in all of you
will not waver in the slightest.

81
00:04:23,101 --> 00:04:24,869
It's okay, Mr. Onizuka.

82
00:04:24,936 --> 00:04:27,805
If you keep trying,
one day your dream will come true.

83
00:04:27,872 --> 00:04:29,874
You're so positive, Mr. Murayama.

84
00:04:29,941 --> 00:04:33,478
I'm so glad I got you
as one more ally in the staff room!

85
00:04:33,544 --> 00:04:35,480
One more? Who is the other one?

86
00:04:36,814 --> 00:04:39,150
It's you, who else, Ms. Kashiwabara?

87
00:04:39,217 --> 00:04:41,285
Sorry, I have no intention of helping you.

88
00:04:41,853 --> 00:04:43,454
You're being cold again…

89
00:04:43,521 --> 00:04:45,256
Let's do our best today!

90
00:04:54,532 --> 00:04:56,768
Ryunosuke, who were you talking to?

91
00:04:56,834 --> 00:04:58,603
Oh… no one!

92
00:04:58,669 --> 00:05:00,104
More importantly…

93
00:05:00,171 --> 00:05:01,506
Take a look at this.

94
00:05:01,572 --> 00:05:04,041
There's been a new post
by someone in your class.

95
00:05:04,642 --> 00:05:06,711
THIS SCHOOL IS BORING, WHY DON'T WE QUIT?

96
00:05:09,013 --> 00:05:11,783
So that girl earlier was your informant?

97
00:05:12,483 --> 00:05:14,318
Forget about that!

98
00:05:14,385 --> 00:05:17,755
You should be careful. We have
parent-teacher meetings coming up soon.

99
00:05:17,822 --> 00:05:19,290
Well, it'll be fine.

100
00:05:19,357 --> 00:05:22,427
Say what you want, but everyone
in my class is a good kid.

101
00:05:23,294 --> 00:05:28,633
Still, if anything happens,
it might affect your summer bonus.

102
00:05:30,368 --> 00:05:32,570
I'll be careful. Okay?

103
00:07:00,291 --> 00:07:01,792
All right!

104
00:07:01,859 --> 00:07:02,960
Today,

105
00:07:04,195 --> 00:07:09,033
you are a perfect number.
All 28 of you are present.

106
00:07:11,035 --> 00:07:12,003
Huh?

107
00:07:12,637 --> 00:07:15,339
Kotone, do you finally feel
like giving me a good rating?

108
00:07:15,406 --> 00:07:19,377
Sorry. I'm still not entirely
convinced by your methods.

109
00:07:19,443 --> 00:07:23,047
Don't say that.
What's the problem, anyway?

110
00:07:23,948 --> 00:07:28,219
You should trust me!
Don't call the school boring.

111
00:07:28,286 --> 00:07:29,186
What?

112
00:07:29,854 --> 00:07:31,389
Did someone say that?

113
00:07:31,455 --> 00:07:33,858
No, not really.

114
00:07:33,925 --> 00:07:36,694
Mr. Onizuka, may I share the announcement?

115
00:07:36,761 --> 00:07:38,696
Sorry. Go ahead.

116
00:07:38,763 --> 00:07:41,198
We have parent-teacher meetings
starting next week,

117
00:07:41,265 --> 00:07:44,602
so please talk to your parents
and let us know your preferred dates.

118
00:07:44,669 --> 00:07:48,940
Before that,
I want to know your planned career paths,

119
00:07:49,006 --> 00:07:51,742
so starting today,
I'll be hearing from each of you.

120
00:07:51,809 --> 00:07:53,811
Why do we have to do that?

121
00:07:53,878 --> 00:07:56,080
Can't we just discuss them
during the meeting?

122
00:07:56,147 --> 00:07:59,150
I mean, what if we haven't planned
a career path yet?

123
00:07:59,216 --> 00:08:00,785
Then just tell me you don't have one.

124
00:08:00,851 --> 00:08:02,887
Knowing how you feel beforehand

125
00:08:02,954 --> 00:08:05,456
will make it easier for me
when talking to your parents.

126
00:08:05,523 --> 00:08:10,661
That's right, Ms. Kashiwabara and I
are on your side, after all.

127
00:08:15,967 --> 00:08:19,770
Hey, you always mess up at the same part.

128
00:08:19,837 --> 00:08:20,938
Right, Momocchi?

129
00:08:21,005 --> 00:08:22,873
You're always laughing!

130
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:23,975
Hey, Wataru!

131
00:08:24,709 --> 00:08:25,576
What?

132
00:08:25,643 --> 00:08:27,311
Why not eat with us?

133
00:08:27,378 --> 00:08:29,780
You can also join our team
as the fifth member!

134
00:08:30,581 --> 00:08:32,850
Sorry, I'm not interested
in that kind of thing.

135
00:08:36,854 --> 00:08:38,823
I've been wondering this for a while now…

136
00:08:39,323 --> 00:08:42,593
Every day at lunchtime,
he disappears somewhere by himself.

137
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,596
Come to think of it,
I've never seen Wataru eating lunch.

138
00:08:46,163 --> 00:08:48,733
Maybe he's doing something shady.

139
00:08:48,799 --> 00:08:50,101
Should I tail him?

140
00:08:50,167 --> 00:08:51,535
Stop it.

141
00:09:17,094 --> 00:09:18,262
What do you want?

142
00:09:18,329 --> 00:09:19,797
N-Nothing.

143
00:09:19,864 --> 00:09:20,831
I'm sorry!

144
00:10:08,546 --> 00:10:10,581
SCHEDULED DATES
FOR THE PARENT-TEACHER MEETINGS

145
00:10:11,148 --> 00:10:12,883
So, what are your plans as of now?

146
00:10:13,451 --> 00:10:15,352
I'm aiming for a recommended admission.

147
00:10:15,419 --> 00:10:16,253
Me too!

148
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,322
By the way, what did Yuukichi say?

149
00:10:18,389 --> 00:10:20,391
I dream big. I want to go to Stanford!

150
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:22,226
Humanities.
A public university if possible.

151
00:10:22,293 --> 00:10:23,961
Sciences. I'm aiming for Tokyo U.

152
00:10:24,028 --> 00:10:26,630
I'm fine with any school
that will accept me…

153
00:10:26,697 --> 00:10:29,433
It's like I'm going from the J-League
to the Premier League.

154
00:10:30,501 --> 00:10:31,502
I haven't thought about it.

155
00:10:31,569 --> 00:10:34,305
I haven't decided yet.
I'm considering various options.

156
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:39,176
Wataru, I bet you're aiming
for a top university!

157
00:10:39,243 --> 00:10:42,413
He hasn't decided whether to go into
science or humanities yet.

158
00:10:43,647 --> 00:10:45,116
I'm quitting.

159
00:10:45,182 --> 00:10:47,351
What? Will you not take entrance exams?

160
00:10:47,418 --> 00:10:48,853
I'm not talking about that.

161
00:10:51,288 --> 00:10:52,056
WITHDRAWAL NOTICE

162
00:10:52,123 --> 00:10:52,790
What?

163
00:10:52,857 --> 00:10:55,593
You can't just suddenly hand me this.

164
00:10:55,659 --> 00:10:56,761
That's right. What is your reason?

165
00:10:56,827 --> 00:10:58,129
It's this…

166
00:11:01,532 --> 00:11:04,368
THIS SCHOOL IS BORING, WHY DON'T WE QUIT?

167
00:11:05,636 --> 00:11:07,638
Did you post this?

168
00:11:07,705 --> 00:11:11,208
No, but I've been
thinking the same thing for a while.

169
00:11:11,776 --> 00:11:14,812
Being at this school isn't fun,
and it's a waste of time.

170
00:11:15,479 --> 00:11:19,150
Don't say that.
Our class is a perfect number, after all.

171
00:11:19,216 --> 00:11:20,317
What?

172
00:11:20,384 --> 00:11:22,720
But I thought you'd support us,
no matter what?

173
00:11:22,787 --> 00:11:23,621
Besides,

174
00:11:24,221 --> 00:11:27,625
in this era, there are other paths
besides going to school.

175
00:11:28,259 --> 00:11:30,294
Well, that might be true, but…

176
00:11:30,928 --> 00:11:34,198
-But, you know, my bonus…
-What?

177
00:11:34,265 --> 00:11:37,234
-No, it's nothing.
-Do your parents know about this?

178
00:11:39,103 --> 00:11:41,972
It has nothing to do with them.
It's my problem.

179
00:11:43,841 --> 00:11:45,643
Hey, Wataru! Hold up!

180
00:11:47,178 --> 00:11:48,913
It's pointless to try to stop me.

181
00:11:51,448 --> 00:11:53,784
Why did he suddenly decide to do this?

182
00:11:53,851 --> 00:11:56,120
I have no idea at all.

183
00:11:56,187 --> 00:11:57,822
Could it be bullying or something?

184
00:11:58,389 --> 00:12:00,658
I don't think it's that.

185
00:12:00,724 --> 00:12:01,859
Are you sure?

186
00:12:01,926 --> 00:12:03,027
What?

187
00:12:03,093 --> 00:12:06,163
Bullying or cliques aren't really
a problem in our class yet.

188
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:09,033
Maybe he lost motivation?

189
00:12:09,099 --> 00:12:10,935
Some are at the top of their class
in middle school,

190
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:13,270
but their ranks drop in high school.

191
00:12:13,337 --> 00:12:16,540
I don't think it's that either.
He studies even during breaks.

192
00:12:16,607 --> 00:12:18,576
Then, is there a problem at home?

193
00:12:19,176 --> 00:12:21,445
I guess that's the only possibility left.

194
00:12:21,512 --> 00:12:23,280
You did contact the guardians, right?

195
00:12:23,347 --> 00:12:24,882
Well, about that…

196
00:12:24,949 --> 00:12:27,685
I've been trying for a while now,
but no one's answering.

197
00:12:28,319 --> 00:12:29,153
What she said.

198
00:12:31,355 --> 00:12:33,490
How pathetic.

199
00:12:33,557 --> 00:12:36,794
It's almost as if you are
Ms. Kashiwabara's assistant.

200
00:12:36,861 --> 00:12:38,929
Well, I thought the same thing.

201
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:43,100
So even you are admitting it?
Do something about it, and quick.

202
00:12:43,601 --> 00:12:46,670
Principal, you give him
a scolding too, for once.

203
00:12:46,737 --> 00:12:48,405
Sure. Well…

204
00:12:49,006 --> 00:12:50,875
-I…
-Mr. Onizuka.

205
00:12:52,509 --> 00:12:53,477
A moment, please?

206
00:12:57,481 --> 00:12:58,782
What's wrong, Ryunosuke?

207
00:12:59,383 --> 00:13:00,751
I got curious and checked,

208
00:13:00,818 --> 00:13:03,854
and it turns out Wataru Tanaka's
tuition and textbook fees

209
00:13:04,488 --> 00:13:07,024
are past the due date and still unpaid.

210
00:13:07,091 --> 00:13:08,692
What, really?

211
00:13:08,759 --> 00:13:10,361
Could that also be a reason?

212
00:13:18,402 --> 00:13:20,170
His pitch yesterday was so fast.

213
00:13:20,237 --> 00:13:22,306
Right? That guy is super strong.

214
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,341
I told you, right?

215
00:13:24,408 --> 00:13:25,542
It's insane.

216
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:42,927
TANAKA

217
00:13:48,966 --> 00:13:49,967
I'm home.

218
00:13:52,937 --> 00:13:55,339
Welcome home! Wataru, watch TV with me!

219
00:13:56,373 --> 00:13:58,275
I'm busy, so watch it with Chii.

220
00:13:59,076 --> 00:14:01,078
But he won't play with me.

221
00:14:05,783 --> 00:14:08,085
Why don't you study a bit?

222
00:14:08,152 --> 00:14:10,721
Shut up. Quit trying to act
like a good big brother.

223
00:14:31,408 --> 00:14:34,044
Wataru, you're back?

224
00:14:41,752 --> 00:14:42,853
What?

225
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,222
I suddenly got called in
for a night shift.

226
00:14:45,289 --> 00:14:47,157
Can you heat up food and eat together?

227
00:14:48,192 --> 00:14:49,626
What? Again?

228
00:14:50,194 --> 00:14:53,597
The new hire suddenly quit,
so I couldn't refuse.

229
00:14:53,664 --> 00:14:57,234
You should just ignore it.
Your leg hasn't even healed yet.

230
00:14:57,801 --> 00:14:59,036
It's okay.

231
00:14:59,103 --> 00:15:01,338
Anyway, something good happened today.

232
00:15:01,405 --> 00:15:04,675
On my way home,
all the pedestrian crossings were green!

233
00:15:04,742 --> 00:15:07,077
I didn't have to stop once.
Isn't that amazing?

234
00:15:07,144 --> 00:15:08,712
Enough already, just go.

235
00:15:08,779 --> 00:15:09,780
Oh, right.

236
00:15:10,748 --> 00:15:12,416
I bought your favorite furikake topping.

237
00:15:32,169 --> 00:15:35,205
Ms. Tanaka, how are your children doing?

238
00:15:35,272 --> 00:15:36,874
They're fine, thankfully.

239
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:40,077
Hey, I heard your eldest son
gets great grades.

240
00:15:40,144 --> 00:15:42,513
Yes, he's very diligent.

241
00:15:42,579 --> 00:15:45,582
My relatives even say I'm lucky
to have a genius like him!

242
00:15:46,116 --> 00:15:47,117
Oh, my…

243
00:15:47,184 --> 00:15:48,685
MR. ONIZUKA
MISSED CALL

244
00:15:48,752 --> 00:15:49,753
What?

245
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:52,456
So many messages from the school?
What could it be?

246
00:15:58,228 --> 00:16:01,632
I am the mother of Wataru Tanaka
from Class 1-B.

247
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,068
What?

248
00:16:07,538 --> 00:16:13,410
SEISHIN HIGH SCHOOL

249
00:16:19,917 --> 00:16:21,351
Good morning.

250
00:16:22,686 --> 00:16:23,620
Good morning!

251
00:16:26,957 --> 00:16:28,025
Good morning!

252
00:16:31,562 --> 00:16:33,664
What are you doing? Come in already.

253
00:16:34,798 --> 00:16:37,167
Did you accept my notice?

254
00:16:41,338 --> 00:16:42,739
WITHDRAWAL NOTICE

255
00:16:43,707 --> 00:16:45,309
Your mother told me

256
00:16:45,809 --> 00:16:48,979
that she has no plans
of letting you quit school.

257
00:16:49,046 --> 00:16:51,482
I told you! My parents
have nothing to do with this.

258
00:16:52,116 --> 00:16:53,317
Right.

259
00:16:54,518 --> 00:16:57,054
What did your father say, then?

260
00:16:57,121 --> 00:16:58,055
Come on.

261
00:16:58,655 --> 00:16:59,623
Well…

262
00:17:00,257 --> 00:17:03,760
He left right after you entered high
school, right? Leaving behind debts.

263
00:17:06,463 --> 00:17:08,966
After that, your mother started working,

264
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:12,870
but her pay is low,
and she recently got injured at work.

265
00:17:12,936 --> 00:17:15,706
She doesn't know
if she'll get workers' compensation,

266
00:17:15,772 --> 00:17:17,040
so things are tough.

267
00:17:18,108 --> 00:17:20,978
-Did she tell you everything?
-Come on now.

268
00:17:21,545 --> 00:17:24,081
Is that why you want to quit school
and start working?

269
00:17:24,615 --> 00:17:26,083
What other choice do I have?

270
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:27,818
My siblings are still young.

271
00:17:27,885 --> 00:17:29,386
Tuition here isn't cheap.

272
00:17:29,453 --> 00:17:33,891
And besides, even if I go to university,
I can't get into a great company anyway.

273
00:17:33,957 --> 00:17:35,325
Why not start working now?

274
00:17:35,392 --> 00:17:37,194
Don't be like that.

275
00:17:37,261 --> 00:17:40,330
We'll discuss it with your mom
at the parent-teacher meeting.

276
00:17:40,397 --> 00:17:41,999
I'll hold on to this for now.

277
00:17:45,369 --> 00:17:46,570
Come on, let's go.

278
00:17:53,043 --> 00:17:53,911
CLASS 1-B

279
00:17:53,977 --> 00:17:56,914
The schedule for the parent-teacher
meetings has been decided,

280
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:57,915
so check your tablets.

281
00:18:04,454 --> 00:18:06,290
Hey, Wataru. What are you doing?

282
00:18:10,027 --> 00:18:13,430
That kind of stuff
has nothing to do with me anymore.

283
00:18:14,331 --> 00:18:15,999
What did you say…

284
00:18:16,066 --> 00:18:18,335
Mr. Onizuka, you can't get violent.

285
00:18:18,402 --> 00:18:20,237
I know that.

286
00:18:20,304 --> 00:18:22,239
Everyone, I'm sorry.

287
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,875
I'm quitting this school.

288
00:18:25,776 --> 00:18:28,946
I don't know if high-tech classes
are your selling point or whatever,

289
00:18:29,713 --> 00:18:31,515
but making us use these devices…

290
00:18:31,582 --> 00:18:33,584
In the end, you just want
to control us, right?

291
00:18:35,285 --> 00:18:38,655
The person who wrote this post
probably thinks the same way too.

292
00:18:38,722 --> 00:18:40,857
Why don't you just step forward?

293
00:18:41,358 --> 00:18:43,460
Instead of making posts like this.

294
00:18:43,527 --> 00:18:46,530
Wataru, enough. The others
have nothing to do with this.

295
00:18:46,597 --> 00:18:47,864
Mr. Onizuka.

296
00:18:47,931 --> 00:18:50,200
Yeah, I know.

297
00:19:03,547 --> 00:19:04,448
Wataru.

298
00:19:05,949 --> 00:19:10,954
If you leave school like this now,
I'm sure you'll regret it.

299
00:19:12,122 --> 00:19:15,559
I also quit high school
because I was sick of it,

300
00:19:15,626 --> 00:19:19,129
but in the end, I wish I had graduated.

301
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:22,666
Because by doing so, I would have made

302
00:19:22,733 --> 00:19:25,102
many good friends,
just like everyone here.

303
00:19:26,970 --> 00:19:28,839
When you say such fake things

304
00:19:28,905 --> 00:19:32,342
with that fake smile of yours,
it makes me want to quit even more.

305
00:19:35,312 --> 00:19:36,446
What did you say?

306
00:19:38,749 --> 00:19:40,484
I'm genuinely worried about you…

307
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:41,752
Mr. Onizuka.

308
00:19:44,655 --> 00:19:46,089
I know that.

309
00:19:51,561 --> 00:19:53,096
If you're going to say that,

310
00:19:53,697 --> 00:19:56,433
I'll make it so you'll
want to stay at this school.

311
00:19:57,334 --> 00:19:59,036
Before the parent-teacher meeting.

312
00:20:00,337 --> 00:20:01,171
What?

313
00:20:01,738 --> 00:20:05,075
If I can do that,
you'll stop trying to quit school.

314
00:20:05,842 --> 00:20:07,544
Got it, Wataru?

315
00:20:13,116 --> 00:20:15,018
Are you sure you can really do it?

316
00:20:15,085 --> 00:20:18,055
Leave it to me,
I'm already thinking up strategies.

317
00:20:18,121 --> 00:20:20,991
By the way, please don't ask me
to participate.

318
00:20:22,259 --> 00:20:25,962
Don't say that. Lend me your wisdom!

319
00:20:39,743 --> 00:20:40,744
Wataru.

320
00:20:40,811 --> 00:20:41,645
OPERATION MAKE FRIENDS

321
00:20:41,712 --> 00:20:44,481
The Drill Team wants to talk to you.

322
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:50,987
Hey, Wataru.
Don't say you're going to quit.

323
00:20:51,054 --> 00:20:54,758
Yeah, that's right. We need you
to help us with our studies too.

324
00:20:54,825 --> 00:20:57,728
Won't you do drills with us?

325
00:20:57,794 --> 00:20:59,930
Having to say goodbye like this…
Is just too sad.

326
00:21:08,171 --> 00:21:09,239
How about it, Wataru?

327
00:21:09,306 --> 00:21:11,575
Your feelings
aren't coming through at all.

328
00:21:12,142 --> 00:21:14,344
The last two
were totally reading from a script.

329
00:21:32,062 --> 00:21:34,765
This time, Mr. Murayama
wants to talk to you.

330
00:21:34,831 --> 00:21:35,999
OPERATION WONDERFUL TEACHER

331
00:21:36,066 --> 00:21:38,568
Your desire to help your mother is noble,

332
00:21:38,635 --> 00:21:41,438
but at your age,
you still have a lot to learn.

333
00:21:41,505 --> 00:21:43,640
It's best to focus on your studies.

334
00:21:43,707 --> 00:21:45,442
We'll do all we can to help.

335
00:21:45,509 --> 00:21:47,744
That's right! What a counselor you are!

336
00:21:47,811 --> 00:21:49,246
Then let me ask you…

337
00:21:49,746 --> 00:21:52,315
Why do we have to study
in the first place?

338
00:21:53,116 --> 00:21:54,785
-Well…
-It's to…

339
00:21:54,851 --> 00:21:58,155
Don't tell me it's to get into
a good company or a good university.

340
00:21:58,221 --> 00:22:00,357
Well, then, it's to…

341
00:22:00,424 --> 00:22:01,792
To understand the world.

342
00:22:01,858 --> 00:22:04,861
If you learn the knowledge humanity
has accumulated throughout history,

343
00:22:04,928 --> 00:22:08,198
I'm sure it will help you in the future.

344
00:22:08,265 --> 00:22:11,601
I can look up that kind of thing
on the Internet, can't I?

345
00:22:38,662 --> 00:22:40,030
Thanks.

346
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:44,401
Hey, Wataru.

347
00:22:46,436 --> 00:22:49,473
Mr. Ryunosuke Miyazawa
has good news for you.

348
00:22:49,539 --> 00:22:53,243
-He is from the company that manages our…
-I know.

349
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:55,178
Well, that's great.

350
00:22:55,745 --> 00:22:59,015
Wataru, if you're worried
about financial matters,

351
00:22:59,082 --> 00:23:02,352
you know that high school tuition
has essentially become free, right?

352
00:23:02,986 --> 00:23:04,621
What, really?

353
00:23:04,688 --> 00:23:06,623
Isn't that great, Wataru?

354
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:10,293
You call it free, but it actually costs
about 450,000 yen.

355
00:23:11,161 --> 00:23:13,396
As ours is a private school,
it's double that per year.

356
00:23:14,531 --> 00:23:16,066
Really, Ryunosuke?

357
00:23:17,434 --> 00:23:18,568
It's all right.

358
00:23:18,635 --> 00:23:21,771
Our company also has a scholarship system.

359
00:23:22,772 --> 00:23:26,009
See, now you don't have to worry anymore.

360
00:23:27,711 --> 00:23:31,715
I can get through high school,
but university costs way more.

361
00:23:31,781 --> 00:23:35,418
And besides, scholarships
are ultimately just debt, aren't they?

362
00:23:36,086 --> 00:23:39,723
Your company's successful, so don't
be stingy and just give it for free!

363
00:23:39,789 --> 00:23:42,092
-Don't phrase it like that…
-Just leave me alone.

364
00:23:43,093 --> 00:23:46,830
Even if you ask people to help or use
cheap tricks, it won't change my mind.

365
00:23:46,897 --> 00:23:50,000
In the end, you just want
high ratings and your bonus.

366
00:23:50,066 --> 00:23:52,002
It's why you don't want me to quit, right?

367
00:23:52,569 --> 00:23:53,403
Wait, you!

368
00:23:53,470 --> 00:23:55,839
-You've been nothing but a miserable…
-Hey!

369
00:23:55,906 --> 00:23:58,475
I don't care about things like bonuses!

370
00:24:01,144 --> 00:24:02,445
Wataru!

371
00:24:06,149 --> 00:24:07,551
I finally defeated them!

372
00:24:07,617 --> 00:24:10,020
-Finally?
-Yeah, I finally did it.

373
00:24:16,126 --> 00:24:17,661
-Hey!
-What are you doing?

374
00:24:18,461 --> 00:24:20,497
You're annoying. Get out of my way!

375
00:24:35,111 --> 00:24:36,613
Oh, hello.

376
00:24:39,950 --> 00:24:42,586
Hey Wataru, are you okay?

377
00:24:45,221 --> 00:24:47,390
-Why are you here?
-Well…

378
00:24:47,457 --> 00:24:49,559
Your mother called.

379
00:24:50,427 --> 00:24:52,929
She said she's working
and couldn't come pick you up.

380
00:24:55,065 --> 00:24:57,767
I'm so sorry for causing you trouble.

381
00:24:57,834 --> 00:25:02,672
It's fine, fortunately,
they weren't severely injured,

382
00:25:02,739 --> 00:25:05,241
so if he apologizes, it should be fine.

383
00:25:05,909 --> 00:25:08,411
I see, thank you very much.

384
00:25:09,613 --> 00:25:12,182
Wataru. Why don't you
apologize to your mother?

385
00:25:12,882 --> 00:25:14,117
You made her worry.

386
00:25:15,051 --> 00:25:16,052
It's all right.

387
00:25:16,653 --> 00:25:18,955
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

388
00:25:21,725 --> 00:25:25,195
I'm sorry. I know
you were worried about me.

389
00:25:26,129 --> 00:25:28,999
Because of me,
my son said he was dropping out…

390
00:25:29,065 --> 00:25:31,735
I'm really a useless mother, aren't I?

391
00:25:32,902 --> 00:25:35,872
But I will be fine, you know!

392
00:25:35,939 --> 00:25:39,109
Right, I had some good luck today!

393
00:25:39,175 --> 00:25:42,245
At the supermarket, they gave me
free croquettes and cutlets.

394
00:25:42,312 --> 00:25:45,448
I told you,
quit saying stuff like that already!

395
00:25:46,950 --> 00:25:47,817
What?

396
00:25:48,418 --> 00:25:50,687
I can't stand that side of you anymore.

397
00:25:52,222 --> 00:25:53,423
Wataru.

398
00:25:54,891 --> 00:25:55,925
You…

399
00:25:57,093 --> 00:25:58,328
What did you just say?

400
00:25:59,195 --> 00:26:00,030
Huh?

401
00:26:01,131 --> 00:26:04,300
Are you so mighty now,
you don't even call her "Mom" anymore?

402
00:26:05,502 --> 00:26:06,636
I'll tell you something.

403
00:26:07,470 --> 00:26:10,640
Your mother is way more incredible
than someone like you.

404
00:26:11,241 --> 00:26:12,542
Every single day, without fail,

405
00:26:13,143 --> 00:26:16,980
she makes meals for her kids,
does the cleaning and laundry.

406
00:26:17,547 --> 00:26:19,349
She asks for nothing in return.

407
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:21,584
Don't you think she's amazing?

408
00:26:22,585 --> 00:26:24,788
I'm sorry, Mr. Onizuka. Because of me…

409
00:26:26,389 --> 00:26:29,359
Parents apologize like this!

410
00:26:29,926 --> 00:26:32,028
They'll do whatever it takes
for their kids.

411
00:26:33,029 --> 00:26:34,297
And yet here you are.

412
00:26:34,798 --> 00:26:37,233
Don't act like a hotshot,
you're just a damn brat!

413
00:26:39,969 --> 00:26:41,371
It doesn't even matter anymore.

414
00:26:42,372 --> 00:26:43,206
What?

415
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:47,110
I got into a fight!
So I'll be expelled anyway.

416
00:26:47,177 --> 00:26:49,345
Wataru, wait a minute!

417
00:26:52,248 --> 00:26:53,817
Is that true, Mr. Onizuka?

418
00:26:55,318 --> 00:26:57,420
Oh, no…

419
00:27:00,323 --> 00:27:01,791
It's all right.

420
00:27:02,358 --> 00:27:06,529
What happened today,
I won't tell the school about it.

421
00:27:08,098 --> 00:27:09,232
Thank you very much.

422
00:27:15,138 --> 00:27:17,006
It's my fault.

423
00:27:17,574 --> 00:27:19,476
Ever since my husband left,

424
00:27:19,542 --> 00:27:22,312
even when Wataru
wouldn't look me in the eye,

425
00:27:22,979 --> 00:27:25,081
I lacked the confidence to scold him.

426
00:27:26,850 --> 00:27:30,353
Because I can't buy him the things
he wants like other families do,

427
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:33,189
and I can't provide
a satisfying life for him.

428
00:27:35,692 --> 00:27:37,827
-Mom, I'm hungry.
-Me too.

429
00:27:39,095 --> 00:27:41,297
Sorry, I'll make something right now.

430
00:27:45,201 --> 00:27:46,302
Well, then…

431
00:27:46,803 --> 00:27:48,605
I'll be on my way.

432
00:27:55,612 --> 00:27:56,579
So sleepy.

433
00:27:57,147 --> 00:27:58,581
-Hey, Onizuka!
-What?

434
00:27:58,648 --> 00:28:02,585
Why didn't you report to me?
A student in your class got violent!

435
00:28:02,652 --> 00:28:05,188
-What are you talking about?
-Don't play dumb, look!

436
00:28:07,023 --> 00:28:10,693
"A violent incident.
Is expulsion necessary?"

437
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,195
Who posted this?

438
00:28:12,262 --> 00:28:14,964
Probably Wataru himself.
Since he wants to be expelled.

439
00:28:15,865 --> 00:28:17,967
Wataru…

440
00:28:19,636 --> 00:28:23,740
For a student of our school
to get into trouble with the police…

441
00:28:23,807 --> 00:28:25,408
It's a serious issue, right Principal?

442
00:28:25,475 --> 00:28:27,243
I suppose so.

443
00:28:27,310 --> 00:28:30,246
Violent students must be punished harshly.

444
00:28:30,313 --> 00:28:32,849
A suspension is too lenient.
This warrants expulsion!

445
00:28:32,916 --> 00:28:35,919
Wataru just wanted to protect
his family as the eldest son,

446
00:28:35,985 --> 00:28:38,288
he wants to get expelled so he can work…

447
00:28:38,354 --> 00:28:41,558
Then why not just let him quit?

448
00:28:41,624 --> 00:28:44,627
He hasn't paid tuition
and textbook fees, right, Principal?

449
00:28:44,694 --> 00:28:46,529
Well, he hasn't, but…

450
00:28:46,596 --> 00:28:48,097
But what?

451
00:28:48,164 --> 00:28:52,735
No, I just think the most wonderful thing
about this school is…

452
00:28:52,802 --> 00:28:56,840
Teaching the importance
of properly following the rules.

453
00:28:58,308 --> 00:29:03,880
Until an official punishment is decided,
that student must remain at home. Got it?

454
00:29:03,947 --> 00:29:04,981
Wait a moment.

455
00:29:05,048 --> 00:29:06,883
I'll talk to him again,

456
00:29:06,950 --> 00:29:09,219
and make him apologize
to the other family.

457
00:29:10,386 --> 00:29:11,955
Everyone, class is about to start.

458
00:29:12,021 --> 00:29:14,891
Are you listening to me? Vice Principal!

459
00:29:16,326 --> 00:29:19,329
What do you think we should do,
Ms. Kashiwabara?

460
00:29:19,395 --> 00:29:23,066
If Wataru's gotten this stubborn,
I think persuading him won't be easy.

461
00:29:23,132 --> 00:29:25,201
Don't say that, please, I'm begging you.

462
00:29:25,268 --> 00:29:29,472
-Begging me to do what?
-Well, if you talk to him…

463
00:29:29,539 --> 00:29:31,774
I think he'll actually listen.

464
00:29:31,841 --> 00:29:34,077
Give me a break, please.

465
00:29:34,143 --> 00:29:35,912
It'll be fine.

466
00:29:35,979 --> 00:29:38,648
You always say profound things,
Ms. Kashiwabara.

467
00:29:39,482 --> 00:29:44,854
Besides, if I go alone,
I might end up punching him this time.

468
00:29:44,921 --> 00:29:47,557
If that happens, I'll get fired,

469
00:29:48,157 --> 00:29:50,493
and you'll become the homeroom teacher.

470
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:51,761
Do you want that?

471
00:29:51,828 --> 00:29:53,763
Is that a threat?

472
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:55,298
Please!

473
00:29:56,299 --> 00:29:57,166
Okay?

474
00:29:57,233 --> 00:29:59,202
TANAKA

475
00:30:03,072 --> 00:30:06,209
I brought you some
school lunch bread… Just kidding.

476
00:30:06,276 --> 00:30:07,810
You're persistent. What is it?

477
00:30:07,877 --> 00:30:09,345
Oh, wait a minute.

478
00:30:09,412 --> 00:30:12,882
Ms. Kashiwabara wants to talk to you.

479
00:30:12,949 --> 00:30:14,384
Miss, come in.

480
00:30:20,890 --> 00:30:24,727
The other day,
it seems you asked why we have to study.

481
00:30:25,428 --> 00:30:27,697
I think it's to acquire a weapon.

482
00:30:28,898 --> 00:30:29,732
What?

483
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:34,137
They say, "Knowledge
is the ultimate weapon of the powerless."

484
00:30:35,538 --> 00:30:39,976
Since ancient times, people who grew up
in poor circumstances used knowledge

485
00:30:40,043 --> 00:30:43,413
to overcome various problems
and achieve their dreams and hopes.

486
00:30:43,479 --> 00:30:45,715
But, these days, I can just search online…

487
00:30:45,782 --> 00:30:48,384
Searching only shows you
things you're interested in.

488
00:30:48,451 --> 00:30:49,986
You'll limit yourself.

489
00:30:51,054 --> 00:30:52,255
However,

490
00:30:52,322 --> 00:30:55,892
school teaches you subjects
you had zero interest in before.

491
00:30:55,959 --> 00:30:59,262
Among them, you might discover
new things to be interested in,

492
00:30:59,329 --> 00:31:02,131
which could turn into a lifelong career.

493
00:31:02,699 --> 00:31:05,601
That's why you shouldn't
rob yourself of that possibility.

494
00:31:05,668 --> 00:31:08,338
Ms. Kashiwabara, you really are profound!

495
00:31:09,238 --> 00:31:11,474
I bet you don't actually care
about me at all.

496
00:31:12,175 --> 00:31:13,042
What?

497
00:31:13,109 --> 00:31:15,878
You talk high and mighty,
like a model teacher,

498
00:31:15,945 --> 00:31:18,414
but it's obvious that you
think I'm just a hassle.

499
00:31:19,048 --> 00:31:21,918
What are you saying?
No way she thinks that. Right?

500
00:31:21,985 --> 00:31:23,453
No, he's spot on.

501
00:31:23,519 --> 00:31:24,354
What?

502
00:31:24,954 --> 00:31:27,357
Honestly, I don't want to do
this kind of thing.

503
00:31:27,423 --> 00:31:29,425
If he quits, my workload would decrease.

504
00:31:29,492 --> 00:31:31,327
Let's let this brat do what he wants.

505
00:31:31,394 --> 00:31:34,063
Quit. Just go ahead and quit!
We don't need you!

506
00:31:34,130 --> 00:31:36,232
Stop, Ms. Kashiwabara! Why agree with him?

507
00:31:36,299 --> 00:31:37,600
Sorry.

508
00:31:37,667 --> 00:31:39,736
Could both of you please go home?

509
00:31:39,802 --> 00:31:41,871
Please just leave already. Leave!

510
00:31:41,938 --> 00:31:43,573
All right, I'm leaving.

511
00:31:46,442 --> 00:31:49,612
Let's have one final lesson. Okay?

512
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:51,614
What?

513
00:31:57,253 --> 00:31:59,389
CLASS 1-B

514
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:02,558
All right.

515
00:32:03,926 --> 00:32:05,528
This should do it.

516
00:32:06,696 --> 00:32:07,730
What are you planning?

517
00:32:09,899 --> 00:32:12,335
I finally remembered.

518
00:32:13,236 --> 00:32:14,103
Remembered what?

519
00:32:15,004 --> 00:32:18,574
When I was around your age,

520
00:32:18,641 --> 00:32:22,145
I used to be so pissed off
at school and my parents.

521
00:32:22,211 --> 00:32:25,048
But since I couldn't express
my feelings well,

522
00:32:25,615 --> 00:32:27,750
I just caused trouble for no reason.

523
00:32:29,786 --> 00:32:31,254
So Wataru,

524
00:32:32,488 --> 00:32:33,456
punch me.

525
00:32:34,357 --> 00:32:35,191
What?

526
00:32:35,925 --> 00:32:37,160
From now on,

527
00:32:37,226 --> 00:32:41,230
whenever you want to go wild,
I will take you on anytime.

528
00:32:42,065 --> 00:32:43,032
So go at it.

529
00:32:44,233 --> 00:32:45,168
What are you saying?

530
00:32:45,234 --> 00:32:47,770
Don't worry. I won't hit you back.

531
00:32:47,837 --> 00:32:50,840
Oh, spare my face, okay?

532
00:32:51,574 --> 00:32:52,608
My wife would be sad.

533
00:32:53,609 --> 00:32:55,511
Aim for the body. The body!

534
00:32:55,578 --> 00:32:57,713
When you get into fights,
that hurts the most.

535
00:32:58,848 --> 00:33:00,917
You say that, but you'll hit back, right?

536
00:33:00,983 --> 00:33:04,754
I won't! In English, they call this…

537
00:33:04,821 --> 00:33:06,355
You know…

538
00:33:06,422 --> 00:33:08,758
-Anger management, right?
-Right!

539
00:33:09,892 --> 00:33:11,494
Don't hold back.

540
00:33:13,629 --> 00:33:14,664
Wataru,

541
00:33:15,431 --> 00:33:19,168
I bet you hate me anyway, right?

542
00:33:28,845 --> 00:33:30,379
I don't feel a thing!

543
00:33:31,247 --> 00:33:32,615
What are you, a girl?

544
00:33:34,450 --> 00:33:37,386
Saying things like that
is sexist, you know.

545
00:33:39,155 --> 00:33:43,726
With weak punches like that,
you won't knock anyone down!

546
00:33:49,065 --> 00:33:49,966
Don't mess with me!

547
00:33:50,666 --> 00:33:52,401
That hurt, you jerk!

548
00:33:52,468 --> 00:33:54,704
You said you wouldn't punch back!

549
00:33:54,770 --> 00:33:56,272
You hit my face!

550
00:33:56,806 --> 00:33:59,408
Besides, your punches are way too soft!

551
00:33:59,942 --> 00:34:02,478
Come at me
like you want to actually beat me up!

552
00:34:02,545 --> 00:34:05,915
With that kind of attitude,
you won't be able to protect your family!

553
00:34:15,291 --> 00:34:16,292
That's good.

554
00:34:17,026 --> 00:34:18,060
Give me more.

555
00:34:21,764 --> 00:34:23,733
I don't care about my family!

556
00:34:23,799 --> 00:34:26,269
My father ran off, leaving behind debt.

557
00:34:26,335 --> 00:34:29,005
My mother acts like a fool
and tries to stay positive,

558
00:34:29,071 --> 00:34:30,640
so I thought I shouldn't complain…

559
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:33,576
I always hide my lunch from my classmates.

560
00:34:34,377 --> 00:34:37,647
I don't even like furikake!

561
00:34:39,415 --> 00:34:42,351
I want to eat steak or ramen,

562
00:34:42,418 --> 00:34:45,555
the expensive stuff,
like everyone else gets to!

563
00:34:47,757 --> 00:34:48,891
That's it, Wataru!

564
00:34:50,860 --> 00:34:53,362
But I'm the eldest son,

565
00:34:53,930 --> 00:34:57,366
and I have to do
something for my siblings.

566
00:34:58,334 --> 00:35:02,071
So I should quit school and help out.
What other choice do I have?

567
00:35:07,543 --> 00:35:08,744
Hit me more!

568
00:35:15,017 --> 00:35:18,287
Everything frustrates me!

569
00:35:19,589 --> 00:35:23,559
When I see people at school having fun,
it pisses me off so much!

570
00:35:25,461 --> 00:35:28,931
When my family
refers to me as the big brother

571
00:35:29,498 --> 00:35:31,634
I feel like destroying everything!

572
00:35:32,802 --> 00:35:36,973
I feel like I'm becoming
more horrible every single day!

573
00:35:37,607 --> 00:35:38,441
But…

574
00:35:39,742 --> 00:35:41,777
I don't know what I'm supposed to do!

575
00:35:43,179 --> 00:35:44,480
Then hit me harder!

576
00:35:47,583 --> 00:35:51,187
Screw you! Screw you!

577
00:35:51,254 --> 00:35:52,121
Come on!

578
00:35:52,188 --> 00:35:53,856
Harder!

579
00:35:55,858 --> 00:35:59,595
Screw you! Screw you!

580
00:36:07,169 --> 00:36:08,437
It hurts…

581
00:36:12,174 --> 00:36:14,577
That last one was something.

582
00:36:15,177 --> 00:36:16,312
Are you all right?

583
00:36:16,379 --> 00:36:17,680
-I'm not.
-What?

584
00:36:18,514 --> 00:36:21,784
Ms. Kashiwabara, please deliver
the closing words for me.

585
00:36:21,851 --> 00:36:23,653
What are you talking about?

586
00:36:23,719 --> 00:36:28,858
You snapped at Wataru earlier.
You want to make up for it, right?

587
00:36:39,502 --> 00:36:41,404
I think your worst flaw

588
00:36:42,838 --> 00:36:45,241
is not relying on adults.

589
00:36:46,242 --> 00:36:50,112
Adults are there to help children
when they're in trouble.

590
00:36:51,113 --> 00:36:54,583
So don't suffer alone,
just talk to us! About anything!

591
00:36:55,818 --> 00:36:58,187
What your mother wants most

592
00:36:58,254 --> 00:37:00,856
isn't for you to help out
with the family finances.

593
00:37:01,424 --> 00:37:04,493
It's for you to find
what you truly want to do.

594
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:06,228
She wants to cheer you on!

595
00:37:07,530 --> 00:37:08,564
So don't ever

596
00:37:09,198 --> 00:37:11,567
try to shut off
your own path in life again.

597
00:37:28,851 --> 00:37:30,019
The sky

598
00:37:32,088 --> 00:37:33,389
is beautiful,

599
00:37:34,390 --> 00:37:35,324
Wataru.

600
00:37:39,795 --> 00:37:41,464
The clouds are drifting by.

601
00:37:46,035 --> 00:37:47,103
Yes.

602
00:37:50,005 --> 00:37:51,207
Mr. Onizuka,

603
00:37:52,908 --> 00:37:53,843
I…

604
00:37:54,744 --> 00:37:57,546
I don't ever want to punch anyone again.

605
00:38:01,117 --> 00:38:02,418
Sounds good.

606
00:38:23,239 --> 00:38:26,041
We are truly sorry for what happened.

607
00:38:26,108 --> 00:38:28,978
He also sincerely regrets what he did.

608
00:38:31,213 --> 00:38:33,449
I am truly sorry.

609
00:38:35,184 --> 00:38:36,485
-I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry.

610
00:38:36,552 --> 00:38:38,487
-Sorry.
-Bad timing…

611
00:38:39,021 --> 00:38:40,956
We'll take our leave.

612
00:38:43,592 --> 00:38:46,996
That was nerve-wracking.
Wataru, were you really that hungry?

613
00:38:47,062 --> 00:38:48,764
Stop deflecting, it was you!

614
00:38:48,831 --> 00:38:51,200
You idiot, it wasn't me! What?

615
00:38:51,267 --> 00:38:52,101
Huh?

616
00:38:52,701 --> 00:38:53,536
Then…

617
00:38:54,470 --> 00:38:56,172
I'm sorry, it was me.

618
00:38:58,808 --> 00:39:01,310
CHINESE RESTAURANT
HOUKA

619
00:39:05,414 --> 00:39:07,383
You guys are hungry too!

620
00:39:08,250 --> 00:39:10,486
We worked up a good sweat. Right, Wataru?

621
00:39:10,553 --> 00:39:11,520
Right.

622
00:39:12,087 --> 00:39:13,389
-But…
-What?

623
00:39:13,456 --> 00:39:15,257
Isn't this favoritism?

624
00:39:15,324 --> 00:39:18,360
Oh, it's fine.
Today is Ms. Kashiwabara's treat.

625
00:39:18,427 --> 00:39:19,695
What? I'm treating you?

626
00:39:19,762 --> 00:39:22,231
I'm just kidding! Ouch…

627
00:39:22,865 --> 00:39:24,433
-Are you all right?
-Nope.

628
00:39:24,500 --> 00:39:27,169
I went to the bathroom
to check it out earlier.

629
00:39:27,236 --> 00:39:28,370
It was all bruised. Want to see?

630
00:39:28,437 --> 00:39:29,672
No, thanks.

631
00:39:30,473 --> 00:39:31,941
-I see.
-Yeah.

632
00:39:41,484 --> 00:39:43,219
Have you decided on what you'll do?

633
00:39:43,786 --> 00:39:47,790
I'll apply for the scholarship
Mr. Miyazawa mentioned the other day

634
00:39:48,357 --> 00:39:50,025
and go to university.

635
00:39:50,092 --> 00:39:51,760
Preferably a national university.

636
00:39:52,628 --> 00:39:56,031
I told him there's no need,
but he said he'd get a part-time job.

637
00:39:57,399 --> 00:40:00,169
He's a reliable big brother.
Right, Wataru?

638
00:40:00,936 --> 00:40:01,770
Well, yeah.

639
00:40:01,837 --> 00:40:04,473
Then, you won't try to quit again, right?

640
00:40:05,808 --> 00:40:06,742
No.

641
00:40:08,377 --> 00:40:09,712
Thank goodness.

642
00:40:10,679 --> 00:40:14,483
I think something
really good happened today.

643
00:40:15,851 --> 00:40:19,321
Mr. Onizuka, thank you for everything.

644
00:40:19,388 --> 00:40:21,490
Oh, it was nothing.

645
00:40:23,492 --> 00:40:26,128
But are you okay?

646
00:40:28,097 --> 00:40:29,198
What do you mean?

647
00:40:29,265 --> 00:40:33,702
Do you have a stomachache?
You've been slouching the whole time…

648
00:40:33,769 --> 00:40:35,004
Oh!

649
00:40:37,806 --> 00:40:39,942
I'm totally fine.

650
00:40:42,545 --> 00:40:44,847
We'll be leaving then.

651
00:40:48,751 --> 00:40:50,686
Oh, wait a second.

652
00:40:52,721 --> 00:40:53,722
Call me "Big Bro."

653
00:40:54,290 --> 00:40:56,025
What? What do you mean?

654
00:40:57,159 --> 00:40:58,260
That's my nickname.

655
00:41:00,563 --> 00:41:01,530
Got it.

656
00:41:02,565 --> 00:41:03,399
Big Bro.

657
00:41:21,483 --> 00:41:22,318
Okay.

658
00:41:22,384 --> 00:41:23,452
Thank you.

659
00:41:38,701 --> 00:41:40,336
Hey, Mom?

660
00:41:41,370 --> 00:41:42,404
It's me.

661
00:41:43,305 --> 00:41:46,208
I just felt like calling you.

662
00:41:47,009 --> 00:41:51,213
What? No, I haven't caused any trouble!

663
00:41:51,814 --> 00:41:54,617
Yeah, we're living apart for now.

664
00:41:55,351 --> 00:41:56,986
But we aren't getting a divorce.

665
00:41:58,554 --> 00:42:00,456
Let me speak too, come on.

666
00:42:00,522 --> 00:42:03,092
It's been a while since I last called.

667
00:42:04,393 --> 00:42:05,561
So,

668
00:42:07,162 --> 00:42:08,263
when I was a kid,

669
00:42:09,365 --> 00:42:11,967
I said a lot of awful things
to you, right?

670
00:42:12,034 --> 00:42:12,868
What?

671
00:42:13,502 --> 00:42:17,106
You're busy? Hey, don't hang up!

672
00:42:19,608 --> 00:42:22,911
I was trying to say "thank you"…

673
00:42:24,313 --> 00:42:26,548
How did things go, Mr. Onizuka?

674
00:42:26,615 --> 00:42:28,117
What? How did what go?

675
00:42:28,183 --> 00:42:31,954
You know, that student who said
he was going to drop out.

676
00:42:33,222 --> 00:42:34,923
That issue…

677
00:42:36,692 --> 00:42:37,760
Everything is fine now.

678
00:42:39,928 --> 00:42:41,497
I see.

679
00:42:44,133 --> 00:42:45,701
You know,

680
00:42:46,435 --> 00:42:49,571
I think the most wonderful thing
about this school

681
00:42:49,638 --> 00:42:53,609
is that we haven't had
a single dropout so far.

682
00:42:54,610 --> 00:42:55,611
What?

683
00:42:55,678 --> 00:42:57,846
I checked the records. It's true.

684
00:42:58,347 --> 00:43:00,816
So, I'm relieved.

685
00:43:03,919 --> 00:43:04,853
Mr. Onizuka.

686
00:43:05,721 --> 00:43:06,555
Yes?

687
00:43:06,622 --> 00:43:09,391
I imagine you will run into
all kinds of students, but…

688
00:43:09,458 --> 00:43:10,426
Principal!

689
00:43:10,492 --> 00:43:13,328
What are you doing?
The school inspectors are waiting.

690
00:43:14,430 --> 00:43:15,698
My apologies.

691
00:43:15,764 --> 00:43:18,000
Do your job, please. I'm busy too.

692
00:43:19,034 --> 00:43:19,968
What?

693
00:43:20,035 --> 00:43:21,704
Did this man do something again?

694
00:43:21,770 --> 00:43:23,939
No. Let's go.

695
00:43:24,006 --> 00:43:24,840
Are you sure?

696
00:43:24,907 --> 00:43:26,175
-Yeah, he didn't.
-Really?

697
00:43:27,943 --> 00:43:31,313
He's actually
a pretty decent person, isn't he?

698
00:43:32,748 --> 00:43:33,982
Mr. Onizuka.

699
00:43:34,683 --> 00:43:36,618
Time for the next meeting…

700
00:43:37,853 --> 00:43:38,921
Oh, okay.

701
00:43:38,987 --> 00:43:41,857
Let's get this show on the road!

702
00:43:52,668 --> 00:43:54,937
DOES THIS SCHOOL
EVEN NEED TEACHERS ANYWAY?

703
00:43:59,408 --> 00:44:00,375
Oh!

704
00:44:00,442 --> 00:44:02,711
Next up is you, Itsuki?

705
00:44:04,747 --> 00:44:06,915
Where are your parents?

706
00:44:07,583 --> 00:44:09,585
My parents leave everything up to me.

707
00:44:10,552 --> 00:44:12,688
Oh, I see.

708
00:44:12,755 --> 00:44:17,092
Mr. Itsuki Fukuda,
you want to apply to Tokyo U?

709
00:44:17,159 --> 00:44:20,262
Excuse me. First, I have a request.

710
00:44:20,829 --> 00:44:23,599
Sure, what is it? Don't be shy.

711
00:44:23,665 --> 00:44:25,434
I'll listen, whatever it is.

712
00:44:27,169 --> 00:44:28,237
Then, I want…

713
00:44:29,071 --> 00:44:30,305
another homeroom teacher.

714
00:44:30,372 --> 00:44:32,241
That's all…

715
00:44:33,041 --> 00:44:34,109
What?

716
00:44:34,643 --> 00:44:36,078
What did you just say?

717
00:44:36,645 --> 00:44:39,581
Could you please change
our class's homeroom teacher?

718
00:44:41,016 --> 00:44:42,251
What?

719
00:44:50,058 --> 00:44:51,627
<i>You'll decide through a vote, you say?</i>

720
00:44:51,693 --> 00:44:52,961
Bring it on, then!

721
00:44:53,028 --> 00:44:55,798
<i>Itsuki's saying if he gets threatened,</i>
<i>he'll transfer schools.</i>

722
00:44:55,864 --> 00:44:56,665
<i>Itsuki!</i>

723
00:44:56,732 --> 00:44:58,300
I'm fed up with that school!

724
00:44:58,367 --> 00:45:00,002
<i>Could you give me a break already?</i>

725
00:45:00,068 --> 00:45:02,638
<i>We must show everyone</i>
<i>what's good about Onicchi!</i>

726
00:45:02,704 --> 00:45:05,374
"A wise falcon has a big head."

727
00:45:05,440 --> 00:45:08,243
I just can't respect you.

728
00:45:08,310 --> 00:45:09,978
-Look!
-What?

729
00:45:10,045 --> 00:45:11,780
Made you look, you fool!

730
00:45:11,847 --> 00:45:14,116
Mr. Onizuka, why did you choose this job?

731
00:45:15,884 --> 00:45:18,020
Because I want to stay at school!

732
00:45:18,086 --> 00:45:19,054
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

